                  "blocks": {
                    "text": {
                      "type": "text",
                      "settings": {
                        "text": "<p>They take the blinding edge off oncoming headlights, so you stop squinting into a white blur.</p><p>Here's why it happens. Modern LED headlights are brighter than the old bulbs, and they're bluer too. Blue light scatters inside your eye. That's the haze, and the blind second right after a car passes.</p><p>Amber lenses filter out that harsh blue light. So you get:</p><ul><li>Headlights that don't blind you</li><li>Eyes that bounce back in a blink</li><li>Night drives that don't leave you wiped out</li></ul><p>They won't darken the road like sunglasses. And they're not a cheap yellow tint that just turns white glare into yellow glare.</p>",
                        "width": "100%",
