        "asset": "noxis-night-road.webp",
        "placeholder_label": "Driver's view of a dark road at night, oncoming headlights glaring",
        "ratio": "1 / 1",
        "image_first": false,
        "title": "You Never Decided to Stop Driving at Night",
        "text": "<p>It happened bit by bit. First the <strong>highway after dark</strong>, then <strong>any road you didn't know by heart</strong>, then the 7 pm plans you were suddenly <strong>too tired for</strong>. Nobody sat you down and said your <strong>driving days were shrinking</strong>, and when you brought it up, someone blamed your age. <strong>It isn't your age. Headlights changed</strong>, your eyes didn't, and that's the part you can <strong>actually fix tonight</strong>.</p>",
        "padding_top": 36,
